{"base_rate":0.3328220858895706,"brier":0.23128343558282208,"bss":-0.04157543937708552,"bss_hi":0.06607906213284807,"bss_lo":-0.16723494847885212,"chart":{"base":[349.7,258.4],"fp":[157.7,111.2],"note":{"base":"skill -0.04 — higher than 9% of cities","fp":"low end -4pp, high end +30pp","rel":"promised 10% → rained 5%; promised 95% → rained 67%"},"rel":"127.1,442.7 275.2,372.2 408.5,348.2 536.9,275.1 660.7,174.7"},"country":"KY","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.2126993865030675,"ess":466.26610878375635,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for George Town</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The George Town rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>75%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(4%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 652 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 1.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.04, ranked 196 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(182&ndash;203) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>17%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>28%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>George Town</b> <span class=\"muted\">Cayman Islands</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;33% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 33% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.04</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>182&ndash;203\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>652 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    George Town &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for George Town\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"71.20476190476191,347.3333333333333 116.59492537313432,289.64179104477614 158.08545454545452,238.60606060606062 198.42000000000002,191.33333333333331 232.69619047619048,162.30000000000078 270.964347826087,118.231884057971 308.05827586206897,87.0344827586207 338.607323943662,59.01408450704224 377.595625,29.375 410.23,18.0 410.23,28.70588235294116 377.595625,80.5625 338.607323943662,125.66197183098592 308.05827586206897,168.62068965517244 270.964347826087,207.91304347826087 232.69619047619048,249.11111111111111 198.42000000000002,283.77777777777777 158.08545454545452,315.8181818181818 116.59492537313432,349.4029850746269 71.20476190476191,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"260.85276073619633\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"260.85276073619633\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"71.20476190476191,358.8888888888889 116.59492537313432,365.7014925373134 158.08545454545452,299.27272727272725 198.42000000000002,306.8888888888889 232.69619047619048,295.33333333333337 270.964347826087,271.2173913043478 308.05827586206897,23